# Personal vault content used for dogfood smoke testing (M11) — never
# belongs in this repo's history, even accidentally via a broad `git add`.
/data/

# Overnight fleet-runner operational artifacts (scripts/fleet/
# overnight_runner.sh). Narrowly scoped to files that are regenerated every
# run AND held open across the run's lifetime: overnight-runner.log is
# reopened-by-path and appended to on every log() call, which means a run's
# own git operations (a cohort commit, etc.) replacing this tracked file
# with a new inode silently orphans that fd — this actually happened on
# 2026-07-25, losing the tail of a run's log even though the run itself
# completed fine. overnight-invocation-*.json(.stderr) are per-invocation
# dumps never referenced by name in scripts/fleet/overnight_prompt.md's own
# commit step, so ignoring them is safe.
#
# Deliberately NOT included: docs/agents/logs/OVERNIGHT_HALT.md IS
# `git add`-ed by exact path in overnight_prompt.md's halt-commit step
# (confirmed via `git log`/`git show` on real halt commits) — ignoring it
# would make that `git add` fail inside an unattended session. Likewise
# the structured per-cohort audit trail under docs/agents/logs/<run_id>/
# (manifest.json, workers/*/result.json, verify/*/result.json — see
# docs/agents/runbook.md) stays tracked.
/docs/agents/logs/overnight-runner.log
/docs/agents/logs/overnight-runner-last-exit.md
/docs/agents/logs/overnight-invocation-*.json
/docs/agents/logs/overnight-invocation-*.json.stderr
/scripts/fleet/.stop
/scripts/fleet/.overnight_runner.pid
